  "chapter": {
    "number": 61,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(62) For the end, a Psalm of David for Idithun."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Shall not my soul be subjected to God? for of him is my salvation.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For he is my God, and my savior; my helper, I shall not be moved",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 109
          },
          {
            "text": "very much.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "How long will you⌃ assault a man? you⌃ are all slaughtering as with a bowed wall and a broken hedge.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They only took counsel to set at nothing my honor: I ran in thirst: with their mouth they blessed, but with their heart they cursed. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Nevertheless do you, my soul, be subjected to God; for of him is my patient hope.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For he is my God and my Saviour; my helper, I shall not be moved.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "noteId": 110
          },
          {
            "text": "In God is my salvation and my glory: he is the God of my help, and my hope is in God.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Hope in him, all you⌃ congregation of the people; pour out your hearts before him, for God is our helper. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But the sons of men are vain; the sons of men are false, so as to be deceitful in the balances; they are",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 111
          },
          {
            "text": "all alike formed out of vanity.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Trust not in unrighteousness, and lust not after robberies: if wealth should flow in, set not your heart upon it.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "God has spoken once, and I have heard these two things, that power is of God;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and mercy is your, O Lord; for you will recompense every one according to his works.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 109,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Or, any more.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 61,
          "verse": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 110,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. on.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 61,
          "verse": 7
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 111,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. altogether.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 61,
          "verse": 9
        }
      }
    ]
  },
